#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:62
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introduccion"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:64
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&bovo; is a Gomoku (Connect Five, Five in a row, X and O, etc) game for &kde;. "
"The purpose of this game is to connect five of your own pieces in an unbroken "
"row vertically, horizontally or diagonally. The two participating players "
"alternate on placing their marks on the playing board."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:70
#, no-c-format
msgid "History"
msgstr "Istoric"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Gomoku, from Japanese 五目並べ, gomoku narabe, <quote>line up five</quote>"
", is a traditional oriental board game, dating back to the 8th century. It is "
"played with black and white Go pieces on a Go board, where black takes the "
"first turn."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:72
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It was soon discovered that black had a huge advantage over white, so a lot of "
"variations have been developed. The most common variation is that only five in "
"a row counts as a win, &ie; six in a row (called an overline) does not count. "
"However, &bovo; doesn't use any of these additional rules."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:73
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In Europe the game is traditionally played on a piece of paper, with the first "
"player drawing X's and the second player drawing O's."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:77
#, no-c-format
msgid "Rules"
msgstr "Règlas"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:78
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&bovo; rules are equal to the traditional free-style Gomoku rules, with no "
"additional extra rules. However, the playing board is 22×22, instead of 19×19 "
"as in the traditional Gomoku game."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:80
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For a more fair game, the two players alternate on who begins. The player who "
"begins does so by placing an X anywhere on the playing field. The players will "
"thereafter alternate in placing their marks on the board."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The game is over when one of the player gets at least 5 marks in a row "
"vertically, horizontally or diagonal."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:85
#, no-c-format
msgid "Help for &bovo;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid "First Startup"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:88
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When &bovo; is started the first time, it needs resizing. Resize the game "
"window to desired size, and &bovo; will scale up the playing board."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:89
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The first time &bovo; is started it is launched in demo mode, where two AI "
"players battle each other."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:92
#, no-c-format
msgid "Auto Save"
msgstr "Enregistrament automatic"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:93
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When &bovo; is exited prior to game over, the active game is auto saved. If "
"&bovo; detects an auto saved game at startup, it is restored. If not, &bovo; "
"launches a demo mode."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:97
#, no-c-format
msgid "Starting a New Game"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:98
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can allways start a new game with the <guibutton>New</guibutton> "
"button in the toolbar, the <menuchoice> <guimenu>Game</guimenu><guimenuitem>"
"New</guimenuitem></menuchoice> menu entry in the menubar or with the default "
"shortcut <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>N</keycap></keycombo>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:100
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If a new game is started when a game is already active, it is counted as a "
"loss."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:104
#, no-c-format
msgid "Changing Difficulty"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:105
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Changing the difficulty can be done with the <guilabel>Difficulty</guilabel> "
"drop down box in the right end of the status bar, of from the <menuchoice>"
"<guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Difficulty</guimenuitem></menuchoice> "
"menu in the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:106
#, no-c-format
msgid "The effect of changing difficulty takes place immediately."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:110
#, no-c-format
msgid "Switching Theme"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:111
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can switch the theme of &bovo; from the <menuchoice><guimenu>"
"Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Theme</guimenuitem></menuchoice> "
"menu in the menubar. The theme is then switched immediately."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:115
#, no-c-format
msgid "Animation"
msgstr "Animacion"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:116
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Animation can be switched on or off as you like from the <menuchoice><guimenu>"
"Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Animation</guimenuitem></menuchoice> "
"menu in the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:120
#, no-c-format
msgid "Undo"
msgstr "Anullar"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:121
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you just realized you made a very bad move, you have the possibility to undo "
"your last move from the toolbar, the menubar or with the default undo keyboard "
"shortcut <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>Z</keycap></keycombo>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:122
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can keep on undoing moves until you reaches the beginning of the game."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:126
#, no-c-format
msgid "Get a Hint"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:127
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you don't know what move to make, you can get a hint from the computer "
"player with the <guibutton>Hint</guibutton> button. The game piece suggested by "
"the &bovo; AI then flashes for a brief period of time."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:131
#, no-c-format
msgid "Replay Mode"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:132
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When a game is over, the <guibutton>Replay</guibutton> "
"action is enabled, which starts a replay of the last game."
msgstr ""

